ution time: a moment seconds (time limit is 2 minutes)."], "analysis": "The reported matched-width contrast and bootstrap are not correctly matched/valid. Growth and decline are pooled across the whole time series, so shared time trends can create the contrast; furthermore the bootstrap samples blocks from `idx` (already filtered rows) but applies those positions as original row indices, mixing unrelated observations and invalidating its interval. Also `np.nan_to_num` makes unavailable lag values zero, although the common interval excludes those rows for the primary fit but sensitivity eval may have distinct masks. Use contiguous original-index moving blocks, and estimate the contrast conditional on width (and time), restricted to genuine support overlap; interpret forecast scores cautiously since expanding TimeSeriesSplit tests later regimes only.", "is_buggy": true}, {"index": 1, "operation": "debug", "plan": "The main bug is that the \u201clagged\u201d model\u2019s features are not actually spline-expanded independently: the pipeline applies `SplineTransformer` to every column, including interaction terms, while the raw change and direction features are poorly specified. The bootstrap also resamples positions from a filtered index list as though they were contiguous, breaking the time-series block structure. The revision uses explicit feature construction, contiguous time blocks, and matched-width contrasts estimated from direction-specific local smooths only over shared support; all scores remain descriptive for this single serial aggregate. It reports sensitivity across prespecified lags and retains the observed-data plot without treating samples as independent replicates.", "exec_time": 0.22814154624938965, "exc_type": "ValueError", "term_out": ["input_rows=2199 missing_required=0 duplicate_timestamps=0", "\n", "usable_rows=2199 time_range_s=(0.0000,7.3267) median_dt_s=0.003333333 regularity_cv=9.97e-14 width_range=(0.0000,17.1456) shear_range=(0.04599,0.21571