mnTransformer requests nonexistent column index 1. Fix by allowing spline_cols=1 for that model (or make design construction handle single-column predictors); then rerun. The reported two earlier scores show the augmented lag model slightly worse than the time+width baseline, but the script terminates before completing diagnostics.", "is_buggy": true}, {"index": 2, "operation": "debug", "plan": "The failure comes from hard-coding two spline columns even when a baseline contains only one feature. I\u2019ll derive spline and linear feature indices from each design matrix\u2019s actual width, so the time-only baseline fits correctly while the two-feature and augmented models retain their intended treatment. The script also keeps the same chronological validation and descriptive interpretation, without treating samples as independent replicates.", "exec_time": 0.5475339889526367, "exc_type": null, "term_out": ["input_rows=2199 missing_required=0 duplicate_timestamps=0", "\n", "usable_rows=2199 time_range_s=(0.0000,7.3267) median_dt_s=0.003333333 regularity_cv=9.97e-14 width_range=(0.0000,17.1456) shear_range=(0.04599,0.21571)", "\n", "blocked_time_width: RMSE=0.009663956 MAE=0.007268262 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_time_width_lagged_change_direction: RMSE=0.009677134 MAE=0.007350481 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_time_only: RMSE=0.01038949 MAE=0.007651518 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_lag_0.05s: RMSE=0.01053883 MAE=0.008081386 n_test=1820", "\n", "blocked_lag_0.10s: RMSE=0.009677134 MAE=0.007350481 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_lag_0.20s: RMSE=0.02332396 MAE=0.01407957 n_test=1780", "\n", "augmented_in_sample_residual_acf1=0.8652", "\n", "matched_width_support=(1.5746,13.4715) growing_n=986 shrinking_n=756 smoothed_growth_minus_decline=0.005050388", "\n", "contiguous_block_bootstrap_raw_contrast_95pct=(-0.00457606,0.001970043) block_samples=30 valid_replicates=500", "\n", "plot_saved=coarsening_shear_memory.png", "\n", "interpretation=descriptive single aggregate; lagged prediction or directional contrast does not establish independent replication or a causal memory mechanism", "\n", "Execution time: a moment seconds (time limit is 2 minutes)."], "analysis": "The execution completes, but the claimed matched-width contrast is not actually conditioned on time: it separately fits growth and decline shear against width, so shared temporal trends can produce the apparent difference. The reported bootstrap interval is for a different unadjusted raw mean contrast, with direction and width range held fixed and resampling indices independently across blocks, so it does not quantify uncertainty for the displayed smoothed contrast or preserve a proper moving-block resample. Also, the lagged augmentation does not improve blocked scores over the baseline (slightly worse RMSE/MAE), and high residual ACF indicates substantial unmodeled serial dependence. Revise the matched contrast to estimate growth-direction effect conditional on both width and time, use a block bootstrap that refits that same estimand, and characterize dependence/validation uncertainty; interpret current output as no predictive evidence for added memory.", "is_buggy": true}, {"index": 3, "operation": "debug", "plan": "The bug is in the uncertainty calculation: the bootstrap resamples raw observations and compares their unadjusted mean shear, so its interval does not quantify the same smoothed, matched-width contrast reported by the main analysis. I\u2019ll resample contiguous blocks of the joint time series and recompute the growth-versus-decline contrast within each replicate, including width-overlap checks. I\u2019ll also use the actual elapsed-time spacing for lag differences and report the bootstrap interval as descriptive uncertainty for this single aggregate, not as replication-level inference.", "exec_time": 0.9975287914276123, "exc_type": null, "term_out": ["input_rows=2199 missing_required=0 duplicate_timestamps=0", "\n", "usable_rows=2199 time_range_s=(0.0000,7.3267) median_dt_s=0.003333333 regularity_cv=9.97e-14 width_range=(0.0000,17.1456) shear_range=(0.04599,0.21571)", "\n", "blocked_time_width: RMSE=0.009663956 MAE=0.007268262 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_time_width_lagged_change_direction: RMSE=0.009677134 MAE=0.007350481 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_time_only: RMSE=0.01038949 MAE=0.007651518 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_lag_0.05s: RMSE=0.01053883 MAE=0.008081386 n_test=1820", "\n", "blocked_lag_0.10s: RMSE=0.009677134 MAE=0.007350481 n_test=1805", "\n", "blocked_lag_0.20s: RMSE=0.02332396 MAE=0.01407957 n_test=1780", "\n", "augmented_in_sample_residual_acf1=0.8652", "\n", "matched_width_support=(1.5746,13.4715) growing_n=986 shrinking_n=756 smoothed_growth_minus_decline=-0.003122128", "\n", "matched_smoothed_contrast_block_bootstrap_95pct=(-0.004902243,0.002571514) block_samples=30 valid_replicates=500", "\n", "plot_saved=coarsening_shear_memory.png", "\n", "interpretation=descriptive single aggregate; prediction improvement or contrast does not establish independent replication or a causal memory mechanism", "\n", "Execution time: a moment seconds (time limit is 2 minutes)."], "analysis": "The analysis has a substantive modeling bug: `fit_predict` places `width` and `time` in the spline transformer but sets `n_smooth = min(2, train_x.shape[1])`; for the time-only baseline, its sole time feature is smooth as intended, but `X_aug` appends lag delta/direction/interaction as linear terms. More importantly, the reported bootstrap contrast resamples rows as blocks but preserves precomputed direction labels, not recomputing lagged deltas on each resampled trajectory; this does not estimate uncertainty for the stated matched growth/decline contrast. The 0.1 s blocks are also shorter than indicated residual dependence (ACF1=0.865), so intervals are not reliable. In addition, expanding-window `TimeSeriesSplit` tests only later periods, confounding validation with temporal regime change; the augmented model does not improve versus the baseline (slightly worse RMSE/MAE), and the contrast CI includes zero. Fix by recomputing direction from each bootstrap block/trajectory with boundary handling, selecting blocks based on residual autocorrelation, and reporting that current evidence does not support predictive memory.", "is_buggy": true}]
